# Tech-Stacks used in AASRA

Frontend / Mobile
Kotlin — primary language for the entire Android app
Jetpack Compose (Material3) — declarative UI toolkit for all screens
Jetpack Navigation Compose — handles the two separate nav graphs (citizen flow vs. authority flow)

Android Speech Recognizer API — voice search/input, locale-aware (BCP-47 tags per selected Indian language)
## Backend / Data :

Firebase Authentication — anonymous sign-in for citizens, email/password for authorities/volunteers
Cloud Firestore — NoSQL database for shelters, rescue requests, safe-status records, safe points, blocked zones
Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) — set up for push notifications (via AasraMessagingService)
Maps & Location
Google Maps Compose SDK — live map with color-coded markers 
(shelters/shops/health centers)
Google Play Services — Fused Location Provider — GPS location detection
Google Maps Directions Intent — one-tap turn-by-turn navigation to any resource
Communication Channels
Android SmsManager API — direct SMS delivery (storm alerts, rescue acknowledgments) — works over basic cellular network without mobile data
Android Intent (ACTION_SENDTO / mailto) — email drafting for the Storm Alert feature
Offline Support
SharedPreferences + Gson — local caching of shelter/resource data, so the app falls back gracefully (live data → cached data → demo data) when there's no connectivity
Networking (for weather integration)
Retrofit2 + Gson Converter — HTTP client for the weather API
OkHttp (logging interceptor) — network layer under Retrofit
Kotlin Coroutines (kotlinx-coroutines-android, -play-services) — async operations throughout (Firestore calls, location fetches, API calls)
Localization
Custom in-house i18n layer (Strings.kt, SupportedLanguages.kt, SpeechLocale.kt) — 11-language support (English + 10 major Indian languages) with a language-switcher UI and matching speech-recognition locale
Build System
Gradle (Kotlin DSL) with version catalogs for plugin/dependency management
Android Gradle Plugin 8.5.0, targeting compileSdk/targetSdk 34, minSdk
